ORGANISE AN EVENT

Work With OCRA

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) wants to build strong relationships with obstacle race organisers throughout Ireland.

Independent race organisers are an essential part of the Irish OCR community.

Events such as Hard as Oak, Rampage, Hell & Back, Spartan and Turf Warrior have provided thousands of people with opportunities to experience obstacle racing in Ireland.

OCRA wants to work alongside organisers to help the wider sport continue to grow.


Already Organise an OCR Event?

You do not need to hand control of your event to OCRA in order to work with us.

There are different levels of involvement depending on what makes sense for the event and organiser.


List Your Event

Race organisers can submit suitable obstacle racing events for inclusion within the OCRA Events Calendar.

Being listed helps athletes discover the event and strengthens the national OCR calendar.

A calendar listing does not automatically mean that an event is sanctioned or approved for international qualification.


OCRA Sanctioning

Organisers interested in a more formal relationship may apply for OCRA sanctioning.

Sanctioning provides an opportunity for the event to work with OCRA around appropriate sporting and technical standards.

The requirements will depend on the type and level of competition.


Qualification Events

OCRA is open to expanding the number of Irish events that can provide qualification opportunities for international competition.

Suitable organisers may apply for an event to be considered for OCRA Qualification Event status.

Qualification status must be agreed in advance and the competition must meet the requirements applicable to that qualification pathway.


National Championships

Established race organisers may also have opportunities to work with OCRA to host an Irish National Championship.

National Championship status requires agreement with OCRA and appropriate competition, technical and officiating standards.


How OCRA and Organisers Can Work Together

Depending on the event, collaboration may include:

- Event calendar listing
- Promotion
- OCRA sanctioning
- Qualification Event status
- Technical Official support
- Competition rules
- National Championship hosting
- Results integration
- Rankings integration
- Club connections
- Athlete communication
- Longer-term partnership opportunities


Why Work Together?

Ireland already has a strong community of independent OCR events.

The aim of OCRA is not to replace those events.

A stronger relationship between the national organisation and race organisers can help create:

- More opportunities for athletes
- Better competition pathways
- A stronger event calendar
- More qualification opportunities
- Better links between recreational and competitive OCR
- Opportunities for clubs and coaches
- Consistent sporting standards where required
- Greater national visibility for obstacle sport


Planning a New Event?

OCRA is also happy to hear from people developing new obstacle sport events.

Speaking with OCRA early may help identify opportunities around:

- Calendar planning
- Competition format
- Technical Officials
- Rules
- Qualification
- Clubs
- Athlete participation
- National Championship development


Get in Touch

Whether you already operate an established OCR event or are developing something new, contact OCRA to discuss how we can work together.


